  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle is centered at \\(O,\\) \\(\\overline{AB}\\) is a diameter and \\(C\\) is a point on the circle with \\(\\angle COB = 50^\\circ.\\) What is the degree measure of \\(\\angle CAB?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(25\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(45\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(50\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(65\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "25"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2010-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Consider the following diagram:\n\nWe have that \\[ \\angle AOC = 180^{\\circ} - 50^{\\circ} = 130^{\\circ}. \\]\n\nSince \\(\\triangle AOC\\) is isosceles, we have that \\[ \\angle CAO = \\dfrac{180^{\\circ} - 130^{\\circ}}{2} = 25^{\\circ}. \\]\n\nSince \\(\\angle CAB = \\angle CAO,\\) we have that \\(\\angle CAB = 25^{\\circ}.\\)\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Relate \\(\\angle COB\\) to \\(\\angle AOC\\)",
        "\\(OA=OC\\), so \\(\\triangle AOC\\) is isosceles"
      ],
